ions in these violations indicate that the process is not following the intended sequence or requirements. For instance, attempting to select a country without first ensuring the user is unregistered or the request has not failed can lead to inconsistencies in the account creation process. Similarly, providing information without verifying the user's registration status or country acceptance can compromise the security and compliance of the account.\n\nConclusion:\nThe audit findings indicate significant deviations from the normative intent of the user account creation process. The low Compliance Score of 0.2748 and the numerous causal violations highlight the need for corrective actions to ensure the process aligns with the intended requirements and regulations. It is essential to address these violations and implement measures to prevent such discrepancies in the future, thereby enhancing the security, compliance, and overall integrity of the user account creation process.",
